/-!
# Universal homeomorphisms at a finite stage of a filtered colimit

Let `A` be a commutative ring and let `B` be a diagram of commutative `A`-algebras over a
filtered index category whose transition maps are surjective, with colimit `B'`. Assume `B'` is
of finite type over `A`, every `B i` is of finite presentation over `A`, and `Spec B' → Spec A`
is a universal homeomorphism. Then `Spec (B j) → Spec A` is a universal homeomorphism for every
sufficiently late index `j`, and the same holds for the stronger property of being a universal
homeomorphism which induces isomorphisms on residue fields.

## Main definitions

No new definitions are introduced.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_isColimit`: the universal
  homeomorphism property holds at every sufficiently late stage.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_universalHomeomorphism_and_isIso_residueFieldMap_of_isColimit`: so
  does the conjunction of that property with inducing isomorphisms on residue fields.

Auxiliary results of independent interest:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_surjective`: a surjection of rings whose
  kernel consists of nilpotents induces a universal homeomorphism on spectra.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_surjective`: a surjection of rings induces
  isomorphisms on all residue fields.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.restrictScalars_adjoin_bot`: adjoining a set over the image of the base ring
  gives the same subring as adjoining it over the base ring.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis "`A → B j` is injective" of the tower criterion of Stacks 0CNE, namely
`universalHomeomorphism_spec_iff_finite_adjoin_tower`, and of the tower criterion of Stacks
0CND, namely `universalHomeomorphism_and_residueFieldIso_iff_finite_adjoin_square_cube`, fails
for the algebras at hand, so, following the source, the base is replaced by the image of `A`,
which is spelled `(⊥ : Subalgebra A _)`. The comparison
between `A` and that image is a surjection with nil kernel, hence a universal homeomorphism with
unchanged residue fields, which is `universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_surjective` together with
`isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_surjective`; the kernel is nil because the morphism on spectra
of `A → B'` is surjective. Changing the base this way changes the subring generated by a set not
at all, which is `restrictScalars_adjoin_bot`, so every tower condition can be read over `A`.

Since the transition maps are surjective, so is every leg of the colimit cocone
(`CommAlgCat.surjective_app`). This is what makes the argument of the source shorter here: the
generators of `B'` produced by the tower criterion lift to *any* stage, rather than only to a
late one, and the finitely many polynomial identities witnessing the tower conditions and the
generation of `B j` then hold at a single late stage by `CommAlgCat.exists_map_eq`. Memberships
in a subring generated by a family are turned into such polynomial identities through
`Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval`, which is the whole purpose of the multivariate
polynomials appearing in `exists_late_stage`.

The index category is allowed to have objects and morphisms in universes unrelated to the
universe of the algebras, which is forced rather than chosen: the intended application has an
index category strictly larger than the algebras.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EUJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EUJ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Changing the base ring to its image -/

/-- Adjoining a set of elements over the image of the base ring gives the same subring as
adjoining it over the base ring itself. -/
lemma restrictScalars_adjoin_bot {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (S : Set B) :
    (Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) S).restrictScalars A = Algebra.adjoin A S := by
  rw [Algebra.restrictScalars_adjoin]
  refine le_antisymm (Algebra.adjoin_le ?_) (Algebra.adjoin_mono Set.subset_union_right)
  rintro x (hx | hx)
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Algebra.mem_bot.mp hx
    exact Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ a
  · exact Algebra.subset_adjoin hx

/-- Membership in the subring generated by a set does not depend on whether the base ring or its
image in the ambient ring is used. -/
lemma mem_adjoin_bot_iff {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    {S : Set B} {x : B} :
    x ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) S ↔ x ∈ Algebra.adjoin A S := by
  rw [← restrictScalars_adjoin_bot (A := A) S]
  exact (Subalgebra.mem_restrictScalars A).symm

/-- The map from the base ring onto its image in an algebra is surjective. -/
lemma surjective_algebraMap_bot (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] :
    Function.Surjective (algebraMap A ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Algebra.mem_bot.mp x.2
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩

/-- The kernel of the map onto the image of the base ring is the kernel of the structure map. -/
lemma ker_algebraMap_bot (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] :
    RingHom.ker (algebraMap A ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)) = RingHom.ker (algebraMap A B) := by
  ext a
  simp only [RingHom.mem_ker]
  exact ⟨congrArg (Subtype.val (p := fun x => x ∈ (⊥ : Subalgebra A B))), fun h => Subtype.ext h⟩

/-! ### Surjections of rings -/

/-- A surjection of commutative rings whose kernel consists of nilpotent elements induces a
universal homeomorphism on spectra. -/
lemma universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_surjective {A C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] (hs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A C))
    (hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A C) ≤ nilradical A) :
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C)).op) := by
  rw [universalHomeomorphism_iff_integral_universallyInjective_surjective]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact IsIntegralHom.SpecMap_iff.mpr (algebraMap_isIntegral_iff.mpr
      (Algebra.isIntegral_def.mpr fun x => by
        obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hs x
        exact isIntegral_algebraMap))
  · have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C))) :=
      IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ hs
    show UniversallyInjective (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C)))
    infer_instance
  · rw [surjective_iff]
    show Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A C))
    rw [← Set.range_eq_univ, _root_.range_comap_of_surjective _ _ hs]
    exact (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_eq_univ_iff _).mpr hker

/-- A surjection of commutative rings induces an isomorphism on the residue field at every
point of the spectrum of the target. -/
lemma isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_surjective {A C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] (hs : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A C)) (x : Spec (.of C)) :
    IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C)).op).residueFieldMap x) := by
  show IsIso ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C))).residueFieldMap x)
  have : x.asIdeal.IsPrime := specPoint_asIdeal_isPrime _ _
  have : (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C)) x).asIdeal.IsPrime :=
    specPoint_asIdeal_isPrime _ _
  exact specResidueFieldMap_isIso_of_idealResidueFieldMap _ _
    ((ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).mpr
      ((RingHom.surjectiveOnStalks_of_surjective hs).residueFieldMap_bijective _ _ _))

/-- The morphism on spectra of `A → B` factors through the spectrum of the image of `A`. -/
private lemma specMap_bot_comp (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] :
    Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)).op ≫
        Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B))).op =
      Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).op := by
  show Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B))) =
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))
  rw [← Spec.map_comp]
  congr 1

/-- If the morphism on spectra of the image of `A` in `B` into `B` is a universal homeomorphism
and the kernel of `A → B` consists of nilpotents, then `Spec B → Spec A` is a universal
homeomorphism. -/
lemma universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_bot {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] (hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A B) ≤ nilradical A)
    (hUH : UniversalHomeomorphism
      (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)).op)) :
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).op) := by
  have hbase : UniversalHomeomorphism
      (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B))).op) :=
    universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_surjective (surjective_algebraMap_bot A B)
      (by rwa [ker_algebraMap_bot])
  have := (universalHomeomorphism_hasTwoOutOfThreeProperty.toIsStableUnderComposition).comp_mem
    _ _ hUH hbase
  rwa [specMap_bot_comp] at this

/-- If the morphism on spectra of the image of `A` in `B` into `B` induces isomorphisms on
residue fields, then so does `Spec B → Spec A`. -/
lemma isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_bot {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B]
    (hres : ∀ x : Spec (.of B), IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)).op).residueFieldMap x))
    (x : Spec (.of B)) :
    IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).op).residueFieldMap x) := by
  rw [← specMap_bot_comp A B, Scheme.residueFieldMap_comp]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso'
    (isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_surjective (surjective_algebraMap_bot A B) _) (hres x)

/-! ### Transporting finitely many identities to a late stage -/

/-- Applying a composite transition map is applying the two maps in turn. -/
private lemma map_comp_apply {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {i j k : J} (f : i ⟶ j) (g : j ⟶ k) (x : F.obj i) :
    F.map (f ≫ g) x = F.map g (F.map f x) := by
  rw [F.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- Finitely many equations between elements of a stage of a filtered diagram of commutative
algebras with surjective transition maps which hold in the colimit already hold simultaneously
at a single finite stage.  Auxiliary version with the equations indexed by `Fin N`. -/
private lemma exists_map_forall_eq_fin {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    [IsFiltered J] {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {c : Cocone F} (hc : IsColimit c)
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f)) {i : J} :
    ∀ {N : ℕ} (x y : Fin N → F.obj i), (∀ m, c.ι.app i (x m) = c.ι.app i (y m)) →
      ∃ (j : J) (f : i ⟶ j), ∀ m, F.map f (x m) = F.map f (y m) := by
  intro N
  induction N with
  | zero => exact fun _ _ _ => ⟨i, 𝟙 i, fun m => m.elim0⟩
  | succ N ih =>
    intro x y h
    obtain ⟨j₁, f₁, h₁⟩ := ih (fun m => x m.castSucc) (fun m => y m.castSucc)
      fun m => h m.castSucc
    obtain ⟨j₂, f₂, h₂⟩ := CommAlgCat.exists_map_eq hsurj hc (h (Fin.last N))
    obtain ⟨l, v, w, hvw⟩ := IsFiltered.span f₁ f₂
    refine ⟨l, f₁ ≫ v, fun m => ?_⟩
    induction m using Fin.lastCases with
    | last => rw [hvw, map_comp_apply, map_comp_apply, h₂]
    | cast m => rw [map_comp_apply, map_comp_apply, h₁ m]

/-- Finitely many equations between elements of a stage of a filtered diagram of commutative
algebras with surjective transition maps which hold in the colimit already hold simultaneously
at a single finite stage. -/
private lemma exists_map_forall_eq {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    [IsFiltered J] {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {c : Cocone F} (hc : IsColimit c)
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f)) {i : J}
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (x y : ι → F.obj i)
    (h : ∀ m, c.ι.app i (x m) = c.ι.app i (y m)) :
    ∃ (j : J) (f : i ⟶ j), ∀ m, F.map f (x m) = F.map f (y m) := by
  obtain ⟨N, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin ι
  obtain ⟨j, f, hf⟩ := exists_map_forall_eq_fin hc hsurj (x ∘ e.symm) (y ∘ e.symm)
    fun m => h (e.symm m)
  refine ⟨j, f, fun m => ?_⟩
  simpa only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.symm_apply_apply] using hf (e m)

/-- Finitely many polynomial identities in the colimit, witnessing memberships in the subalgebras
generated by initial segments of a family and expressing a finite generating set in terms of that
family, already hold at a single late stage. -/
private lemma exists_stage_identities {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    [IsFiltered J] {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {c : Cocone F} (hc : IsColimit c)
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f))
    {i₀ : J} {t : Finset (F.obj i₀)} {n : ℕ} {b' : Fin n → c.pt} {b : Fin n → F.obj i₀}
    (hb : ∀ k, c.ι.app i₀ (b k) = b' k)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (P : ι → MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) (d : ι → Fin n)
    (Q : ∀ m, MvPolynomial {l : Fin n // l < d m} A)
    (hQ : ∀ m, MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b' l) (Q m) =
      MvPolynomial.aeval b' (P m))
    (R : {g // g ∈ t} → MvPolynomial (Fin n) A)
    (hR : ∀ g, MvPolynomial.aeval b' (R g) = c.ι.app i₀ (g : F.obj i₀)) :
    ∃ (i₁ : J) (w : i₀ ⟶ i₁),
      (∀ m : ι, F.map w (MvPolynomial.aeval b (P m)) =
        F.map w (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b l) (Q m))) ∧
      (∀ g : {g // g ∈ t}, F.map w (g : F.obj i₀) =
        F.map w (MvPolynomial.aeval b (R g))) := by
  obtain ⟨i₁, w, hw⟩ := exists_map_forall_eq hc hsurj
    (Sum.elim (fun m => MvPolynomial.aeval b (P m))
      (fun g : {g // g ∈ t} => (g : F.obj i₀)))
    (Sum.elim (fun m => MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b l) (Q m))
      (fun g : {g // g ∈ t} => MvPolynomial.aeval b (R g)))
    (by
      rintro (m | g)
      · show (c.ι.app i₀).hom (MvPolynomial.aeval b (P m)) =
          (c.ι.app i₀).hom
            (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b l) (Q m))
        rw [MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply, MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply]
        simpa only [hb] using (hQ m).symm
      · show (c.ι.app i₀).hom (g : F.obj i₀) =
          (c.ι.app i₀).hom (MvPolynomial.aeval b (R g))
        rw [MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply]
        simpa only [hb] using (hR g).symm)
  exact ⟨i₁, w, fun m => hw (Sum.inl m), fun g => hw (Sum.inr g)⟩

/-- If a surjective algebra map sends a generating set of its source into the subalgebra
generated by a family, then that family generates the target. -/
lemma adjoin_range_eq_top_of_surjective {A S T : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing S] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A S] [Algebra A T] {ψ : S →ₐ[A] T} (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) {t : Set S}
    (ht : Algebra.adjoin A t = ⊤) {ι : Type*} {β : ι → T}
    (h : ∀ g ∈ t, ψ g ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range β)) :
    Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range β) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top ?_
  have htop : (⊤ : Subalgebra A T) = (Algebra.adjoin A t).map ψ := by
    rw [ht, Algebra.map_top]
    exact ((AlgHom.range_eq_top _).mpr hψ).symm
  rw [htop, AlgHom.map_adjoin]
  exact Algebra.adjoin_le (Set.image_subset_iff.mpr h)

/-- Membership in the subalgebra generated by a family is evaluation of a polynomial in it. -/
private lemma mem_adjoin_range_iff_exists_aeval {A T κ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A T] (v : κ → T) (x : T) :
    x ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range v) ↔
      ∃ Q : MvPolynomial κ A, MvPolynomial.aeval v Q = x := by
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval]
  exact AlgHom.mem_range _

/-! ### The late stage carrying the tower -/

/-- The engine behind Stacks 0EUJ.  Suppose `b'` generates the colimit `c.pt` as an `A`-algebra
and finitely many polynomial expressions in `b'` lie in the subalgebras generated by the initial
segments of `b'`.  Then there is an index `i` such that at every later stage `j` one finds a
family `β` generating `F.obj j` for which the same memberships hold. -/
private lemma exists_late_stage {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    [IsFiltered J] {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {c : Cocone F} (hc : IsColimit c)
    (hfp : ∀ i, Algebra.FinitePresentation A (F.obj i))
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f))
    [Algebra.FiniteType A c.pt] {n : ℕ} {b' : Fin n → c.pt}
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range b') = ⊤)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (P : ι → MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) (d : ι → Fin n)
    (hP : ∀ m, MvPolynomial.aeval b' (P m) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b' l)) :
    ∃ i : J, ∀ {j : J} (_ : i ⟶ j), ∃ β : Fin n → F.obj j,
      Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range β) = ⊤ ∧
      ∀ m, MvPolynomial.aeval β (P m) ∈
        Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ β l) := by
  classical
  -- choose a stage and a finite generating set there
  obtain ⟨i₀⟩ : Nonempty J := IsFiltered.nonempty
  have := hfp i₀
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A (F.obj i₀)).out
  -- every leg of the cocone is surjective, so the generators lift to the chosen stage
  choose b hb using fun k : Fin n => CommAlgCat.surjective_app hc hsurj i₀ (b' k)
  -- the witnessing polynomials for the memberships
  have hmem : ∀ m, ∃ Q : MvPolynomial {l : Fin n // l < d m} A,
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b' l) Q =
        MvPolynomial.aeval b' (P m) := by
    exact fun m => (mem_adjoin_range_iff_exists_aeval _ _).mp (hP m)
  choose Q hQ using hmem
  -- the witnessing polynomials expressing the generators of `F.obj i₀` in terms of `b'`
  have hgent : ∀ g : {g // g ∈ t}, ∃ R : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A,
      MvPolynomial.aeval b' R = c.ι.app i₀ (g : F.obj i₀) := by
    exact fun g => (mem_adjoin_range_iff_exists_aeval b' _).mp (hgen ▸ Algebra.mem_top)
  choose R hR using hgent
  -- all of these identities hold at a single late stage
  obtain ⟨i₁, w, hwl, hwr⟩ := exists_stage_identities hc hsurj hb P d Q hQ R hR
  refine ⟨i₁, fun {j} s => ?_⟩
  set ψ : F.obj i₀ ⟶ F.obj j := F.map (w ≫ s) with hψdef
  have hpush : ∀ z z' : F.obj i₀, F.map w z = F.map w z' → ψ z = ψ z' := by
    intro z z' hz
    rw [hψdef, map_comp_apply, map_comp_apply, hz]
  refine ⟨fun k => ψ (b k), ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- the images of `b` generate `F.obj j`
    have hgenj : ∀ g : {g // g ∈ t},
        ψ (g : F.obj i₀) = MvPolynomial.aeval (fun k => ψ (b k)) (R g) := by
      intro g
      rw [hpush _ _ (hwr g)]
      exact MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply b ψ.hom (R g)
    refine adjoin_range_eq_top_of_surjective (ψ := ψ.hom) (hsurj (w ≫ s)) ht fun g hg => ?_
    exact (mem_adjoin_range_iff_exists_aeval _ _).mpr ⟨R ⟨g, hg⟩, (hgenj ⟨g, hg⟩).symm⟩
  · -- the memberships persist
    intro m
    have hid : MvPolynomial.aeval (fun k => ψ (b k)) (P m) =
        MvPolynomial.aeval (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ ψ (b l)) (Q m) := by
      rw [← MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply b ψ.hom (P m),
        ← MvPolynomial.comp_aeval_apply (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < d m} ↦ b l) ψ.hom (Q m)]
      exact hpush _ _ (hwl m)
    exact (mem_adjoin_range_iff_exists_aeval _ _).mpr ⟨Q m, hid.symm⟩

/-! ### Stacks 0EUJ -/

/-- The kernel of the structure map of an algebra whose morphism on spectra is surjective
consists of nilpotent elements. -/
private lemma ker_le_nilradical_of_surjective {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B]
    (h : Surjective (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).op)) :
    RingHom.ker (algebraMap A B) ≤ nilradical A := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A B)) := by
    rwa [surjective_iff] at h
  intro a ha
  have hall : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus ({a} : Set A) = Set.univ := by
    rw [Set.eq_univ_iff_forall]
    intro p
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := hsurj p
    rw [PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus, Set.singleton_subset_iff, PrimeSpectrum.comap_asIdeal]
    exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (by simp [RingHom.mem_ker.mp ha])
  exact (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_eq_univ_iff _).mp hall rfl

/-- The kernel of the structure map of an algebra whose morphism on spectra is a universal
homeomorphism consists of nilpotent elements. -/
private lemma ker_le_nilradical_of_universalHomeomorphism {A B : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)).op)] :
    RingHom.ker (algebraMap A B) ≤ nilradical A :=
  ker_le_nilradical_of_surjective
    ((universalHomeomorphism_iff_integral_universallyInjective_surjective _).mp inferInstance).2.2

/-- A family whose span over the image of `A` contains a generating set of an `A`-algebra
generates that algebra over `A`. -/
private lemma adjoin_range_eq_top_of_subset_adjoin_bot {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] {s : Set B} (hs : Algebra.adjoin A s = ⊤) {ι : Type*} {b : ι → B}
    (h : s ⊆ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) (Set.range b)) :
    Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range b) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top ?_
  rw [← hs]
  exact Algebra.adjoin_le fun x hx => mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp (h hx)

/-- A step of a tower over the image of `A` is witnessed by polynomials over `A` whose shape does
not depend on the algebra in which they are evaluated. -/
private lemma exists_polynomials_of_tower_step {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] {n : ℕ} {b' : Fin n → B} {k : Fin n}
    (h : (b' k ^ 2 ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)
          (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l) ∧
        b' k ^ 3 ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)
          (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l)) ∨
      ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ ((p : B) * b' k ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)
          (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l) ∧
        b' k ^ p ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)
          (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l))) :
    ∃ P₁ P₂ : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A,
      (MvPolynomial.aeval b' P₁ ∈
          Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l) ∧
        MvPolynomial.aeval b' P₂ ∈
          Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l)) ∧
      ∀ {D : Type u} [CommRing D] [Algebra A D] (v : Fin n → D),
        ((MvPolynomial.aeval v P₁ = v k ^ 2 ∧ MvPolynomial.aeval v P₂ = v k ^ 3) ∨
          ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ MvPolynomial.aeval v P₁ = (p : D) * v k ∧
            MvPolynomial.aeval v P₂ = v k ^ p) := by
  rcases h with ⟨h2, h3⟩ | ⟨p, hp, hm, hpow⟩
  · refine ⟨MvPolynomial.X k ^ 2, MvPolynomial.X k ^ 3, ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp h2
    · simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp h3
    · exact fun {D} _ _ v => Or.inl ⟨by simp, by simp⟩
  · refine ⟨(p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) * MvPolynomial.X k, MvPolynomial.X k ^ p,
      ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp hm
    · simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp hpow
    · exact fun {D} _ _ v => Or.inr ⟨p, hp, by simp, by simp⟩

/-- The kernel of the structure map of a stage is contained in the kernel of the structure map
of the colimit. -/
private lemma ker_le_ker_colimit {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J]
    {F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A} {c : Cocone F} (j : J) :
    RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (F.obj j)) ≤ RingHom.ker (algebraMap A c.pt) := by
  intro a ha
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at ha ⊢
  exact ((c.ι.app j).hom.commutes a).symm.trans (by rw [ha, map_zero])

/-- The two index parameterizations of an initial segment of a family give the same range. -/
private lemma range_castLE_eq_range_subtype {D : Type*} {n : ℕ} (v : Fin n → D) (k : Fin n) :
    Set.range (fun l : Fin (k : ℕ) ↦ v (Fin.castLE k.isLt.le l)) =
      Set.range (fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ v l) := by
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨l, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨Fin.castLE k.isLt.le l, l.isLt⟩, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨l, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨l.val.val, l.property⟩, congrArg v (Fin.ext rfl)⟩

/-- A family generating `B` over `A` whose members have square and cube in the subalgebra
generated by their predecessors makes `Spec B` universally homeomorphic, with unchanged residue
fields, to the spectrum of the image of `A`. -/
private lemma universalHomeomorphism_and_isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_bot_of_square_cube
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] {n : ℕ} {β : Fin n → B}
    (hβtop : Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range β) = ⊤)
    (h₂ : ∀ k, MvPolynomial.aeval β ((MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 2) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ β l))
    (h₃ : ∀ k, MvPolynomial.aeval β ((MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 3) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ β l)) :
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map
        (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)).op) ∧
      ∀ x : Spec (.of B), IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map
        (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B) B)).op).residueFieldMap x) := by
  refine (universalHomeomorphism_and_residueFieldIso_iff_finite_adjoin_square_cube
    (A := ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A B)) (B := B) Subtype.val_injective).mpr fun E => ⟨n, β, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact fun x _ => mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (by simp [hβtop])
  · intro k
    rw [range_castLE_eq_range_subtype]
    exact ⟨mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (by simpa only [map_pow, MvPolynomial.aeval_X] using h₂ k),
      mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (by simpa only [map_pow, MvPolynomial.aeval_X] using h₃ k)⟩

/-- **Stacks 0EUJ.** Let a commutative `A`-algebra of finite type be presented as a filtered
colimit of `A`-algebras of finite presentation with surjective transition maps.  If its morphism
on spectra over `Spec A` is a universal homeomorphism, then so is the one of every sufficiently
late stage of the diagram. -/
@[stacks 0EUJ "universal homeomorphism at a finite stage"]
theorem exists_universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_isColimit
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J] [IsFiltered J]
    (F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A) (c : Cocone F) (hc : IsColimit c)
    [Algebra.FiniteType A c.pt]
    (hfp : ∀ i, Algebra.FinitePresentation A (F.obj i))
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f))
    [UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A c.pt)).op)] :
    ∃ i : J, ∀ {j : J} (_ : i ⟶ j),
      UniversalHomeomorphism
        (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (F.obj j))).op) := by
  classical
  have hnil : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A c.pt) ≤ nilradical A :=
    ker_le_nilradical_of_universalHomeomorphism
  -- replace the base by the image of `A` and read off a tower from Stacks 0CNE
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A c.pt).out
  obtain ⟨n, b', hEs, hsteps⟩ :=
    (universalHomeomorphism_spec_iff_finite_adjoin_tower ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A c.pt) c.pt
      Subtype.val_injective).mp (universalHomeomorphism_specMap_to_subalgebra inferInstance _) s
  have hgen := adjoin_range_eq_top_of_subset_adjoin_bot hs hEs
  -- turn the tower conditions into polynomial identities over `A`
  choose P₁ P₂ hPmem hPshape using fun k => exists_polynomials_of_tower_step (hsteps k)
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_late_stage hc hfp hsurj hgen (Sum.elim P₁ P₂)
    (Sum.elim id id) fun | .inl k => (hPmem k).1 | .inr k => (hPmem k).2
  refine ⟨i, fun {j} g => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨β, hβtop, hβmem⟩ := hi g
  refine universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_bot ((ker_le_ker_colimit (c := c) j).trans hnil) ?_
  refine (universalHomeomorphism_spec_iff_finite_adjoin_tower
    ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A (F.obj j)) (F.obj j) Subtype.val_injective).mpr fun E => ⟨n, β, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact fun x _ => mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (by simp [hβtop])
  · intro k
    have hm1 : MvPolynomial.aeval β (P₁ k) ∈
        Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ β l) := hβmem (Sum.inl k)
    have hm2 : MvPolynomial.aeval β (P₂ k) ∈
        Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ β l) := hβmem (Sum.inr k)
    rcases hPshape k β with ⟨e1, e2⟩ | ⟨p, hp, e1, e2⟩
    · exact Or.inl ⟨mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (e1 ▸ hm1), mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (e2 ▸ hm2)⟩
    · exact Or.inr ⟨p, hp, mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (e1 ▸ hm1),
        mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mpr (e2 ▸ hm2)⟩

/-- **Stacks 0EUJ.** Let a commutative `A`-algebra of finite type be presented as a filtered
colimit of `A`-algebras of finite presentation with surjective transition maps.  If its morphism
on spectra over `Spec A` is a universal homeomorphism which induces isomorphisms on residue
fields, then the same holds at every sufficiently late stage of the diagram. -/
@[stacks 0EUJ "universal homeomorphism with equal residue fields at a finite stage"]
theorem exists_universalHomeomorphism_and_isIso_residueFieldMap_of_isColimit
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J] [IsFiltered J]
    (F : J ⥤ CommAlgCat.{u} A) (c : Cocone F) (hc : IsColimit c)
    [Algebra.FiniteType A c.pt]
    (hfp : ∀ i, Algebra.FinitePresentation A (F.obj i))
    (hsurj : ∀ {i j : J} (f : i ⟶ j), Function.Surjective (F.map f))
    [UniversalHomeomorphism (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A c.pt)).op)]
    (hres : ∀ x : Spec (.of c.pt), IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A c.pt)).op).residueFieldMap x)) :
    ∃ i : J, ∀ {j : J} (_ : i ⟶ j),
      UniversalHomeomorphism
          (Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (F.obj j))).op) ∧
        ∀ x : Spec (.of (F.obj j)), IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map
          (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (F.obj j))).op).residueFieldMap x) := by
  classical
  have hnil : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A c.pt) ≤ nilradical A :=
    ker_le_nilradical_of_universalHomeomorphism
  -- replace the base by the image of `A` and read off a tower from Stacks 0CND
  have hresbot : ∀ x : Spec (.of c.pt), IsIso ((Scheme.Spec.map
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A c.pt) c.pt)).op).residueFieldMap x) :=
    isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_to_subalgebra inferInstance hres _
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A c.pt).out
  obtain ⟨n, b', hEs, hsteps⟩ :=
    (universalHomeomorphism_and_residueFieldIso_iff_finite_adjoin_square_cube
      (A := ↥(⊥ : Subalgebra A c.pt)) (B := c.pt) Subtype.val_injective).mp
      ⟨universalHomeomorphism_specMap_to_subalgebra inferInstance _, hresbot⟩ s
  have hgen := adjoin_range_eq_top_of_subset_adjoin_bot hs hEs
  have hPmem : ∀ k : Fin n,
      MvPolynomial.aeval b' ((MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 2) ∈
          Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l) ∧
        MvPolynomial.aeval b' ((MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 3) ∈
          Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range fun l : {l : Fin n // l < k} ↦ b' l) := by
    intro k
    obtain ⟨h2, h3⟩ := hsteps k
    rw [range_castLE_eq_range_subtype] at h2 h3
    exact ⟨by simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp h2, by simpa using mem_adjoin_bot_iff.mp h3⟩
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_late_stage hc hfp hsurj hgen
    (Sum.elim (fun k : Fin n => (MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 2)
      (fun k : Fin n => (MvPolynomial.X k : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A) ^ 3))
    (Sum.elim id id) fun | .inl k => (hPmem k).1 | .inr k => (hPmem k).2
  refine ⟨i, fun {j} g => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨β, hβtop, hβmem⟩ := hi g
  have hboth := universalHomeomorphism_and_isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_bot_of_square_cube
    (A := A) hβtop (fun k => hβmem (Sum.inl k)) fun k => hβmem (Sum.inr k)
  exact ⟨universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_bot ((ker_le_ker_colimit (c := c) j).trans hnil)
    hboth.1, isIso_residueFieldMap_specMap_of_bot hboth.2⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

